data/*.tmp
.env
node_modules

# data/state.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the database: the Clash
# API only serves about ten past river races, so the committed store is the
# only place older history exists. Each scheduled sync commits it, which also
# makes every week's change reviewable in the repo history.

# Build output. CI rebuilds it on every sync; a committed copy only goes stale.
dist/
